Instruction: Read the following segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the timing requirements for representations and warranties under the bring down provision.

Merger Agreement: Section 10.4 Conditions and Representations. The obligations of the Parties to consummate the Merger are subject to the satisfaction, or waiver, at or prior to the Effective Time of the following conditions: 
(a) All representations and warranties set forth in Article VII, except those expressly limited to a specific date, shall be accurate and complete as of the Effective Time, as confirmed by the certificate at Signing; 
(b) Notwithstanding clause (a), any representation for which the Parties do not reserve a revision right pursuant to Section 10.6 must continue to be true as of the Closing Date. 
Furthermore, with the exception of the representations explicitly governed by clause (b), the representations given at the Signing Date shall be deemed conclusive for establishing compliance with the conditions precedent without a subsequent update at Closing.

Question: Based on the provisions above, when are the representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision? Options: Option A: At Signing Only; Option B: At Signing & At Closing.
Choices:
